# Restatement ledger (docs/standards/architecture.md rule 9) for the lane report's field
# labels and the layout that makes them findable, owned by the fenced template in
# .claude/agents/ticket-agent.md rule 8 (#692).
#
# merge-pr.sh does not restate the labels: it reads them from the template at classify,
# a label being what starts an unindented line or follows whitespace on one, so it
# computes with the layout. A field moved onto an indented line, or written without
# whitespace before it, stops being required there and nothing else notices.
# merge-pr.test.sh asserts the list of 16 against a real report (#693's, captured).
owner: .claude/agents/ticket-agent.md
claim: the lane report template's field labels and their layout, which merge-pr.sh derives its required fields from at classify
sweep: rule 8's report template|Footprint drift vs plan comment
scope: :!docs/tech-debt.md :!docs/friction-log.md :!docs/review-feedback.md
carrier: .claude/scripts/merge-pr.sh
carrier: .claude/scripts/merge-pr.test.sh
